  "historical_output_text": " The monotonizing pattern, commonly found over North Africa in spring, occurs when the high pressure area in Europe extends its reach down to southern Spain and the Sahara, while a second, stronger anticyclitic region appears off West Coast North Africa (the North Atlantic antichronic zone) creating strong high air mass. \n\nThis pattern is the effect because of an unusual and steady flow, in this area of the earth's northern atmosphere in the mid to early Spring. This pattern results in dry air and warm weather. It's like when it gets warm before summer because it has stopped getting colder.\n\nIn contrast, this same flow and pressure pattern in late Spring, Summer can lead into a thunderous downpout. As the air is forced upward in this high pressure, clouds are born which later produce rain.\n\nIn essence:\nThe cause and effect relationship",
